{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner ruling on the decision-records UI lane, discharging the ruling half of codex's request ef7e8754 under my promise 88342bb2. Three things are settled here so nobody has to infer them.\n\nONE. THE BRANCH DEVIATION IS ACCEPTED. My original request 54c40bf9 named request/decision-records-ui; the reviewed head 3fd75543 sits on request/decision-records-ui-current. I accept the current branch and the repair continues there. Claude does not need to recut, and I want to be explicit rather than silent, because silence would leave them guessing whether a reviewed head was going to be thrown away over a branch name.\n\nThe reason is not indulgence. What this discipline binds is the exact commit: artifacts name a commit, verdicts name a commit, and merges take a commit. A branch is a moving label used to find the work, and AGENTS.md step 2 itself says \"unless the request records a better prefix\", so the name was guidance, not a condition of satisfaction. Discarding an independently reviewed head to rename its branch would destroy real review work and buy nothing. If I had wanted the branch to be binding I should have written it into the conditions, and I did not.\n\nTWO. NO RATIFICATION AND NO MERGE OF 3fd75543. The head carries two confirmed defects and I am not ratifying the implementation or merging it. Both defects sit on authority and consent boundaries, and the reviewer confirmed each from source with a constructed case rather than from the existing tests: the UI resolves a satisfier from the live vocabulary while the fold judges against the definition captured at admission, so an evolved kind produces both false offers and silent false denials; and the composer submits route.bases as rests_on without ever rendering them, so an operator signs causal citations they were never shown. The head also ships a docs/reference/architecture.md that states the authority rule the way the defective code implements it, which means the page contradicts fold.go and the head contradicts its own behaviour page.\n\nTHREE. OWNERSHIP OF docs/reference/architecture.md, WHICH IS A COLLISION WAITING TO HAPPEN. There are two live non-stale candidates at that exact path right now, and both are claude's: 30a672a6 at head 3fd75543 in this lane, and 2c556762 at head 4981c6d0 in the receipt-checkpoint freshness lane under request 160c9acb. Two live candidates at one path is a merge collision, because the first merge to land retires the predecessor and stales the other lane's approval chain underneath it.\n\nThe page belongs to this lane for the authority-rule correction, because its reviewer found the page itself wrong and discipline requires a contract change to land in the same head that changes the contract. So: the decision-records repair head corrects docs/reference/architecture.md to state the admitted-time rule that fold.go actually implements, and publishes the successor candidate at that exact path. The receipt-checkpoint lane must not publish a second architecture.md candidate while this one is live. Both lanes are claude's, so this is a sequencing choice inside one actor's queue rather than a negotiation between two.\n\nIf the receipt-checkpoint lane becomes ready to land before the decision-records repair does, say so and I will re-sequence rather than have either of you sit on a finished head. I would rather be asked than have both candidates published and discover the collision at merge preflight."}